BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Retreat] Discovery and Developmental Therapeutics (DDT) and Cance
 r Immunology (CI) Joint Program — Breaking Immune Barriers: Translating 
 Discovery into Tomorrow’s Therapies
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260825T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260825T160000
DTSTAMP:20260817T105227Z
UID:winship-4dd1118a2f42f16f14dca73b@emory-seminars
DESCRIPTION:Program: Retreat\n\nSpeaker: Discovery and Developmental Thera
 peutics (DDT) and Cancer Immunology (CI) Joint Program\n\nEvent type: Retr
 eat\n\nTalk title: Breaking Immune Barriers: Translating Discovery into To
 morrow’s Therapies\n\nJoin us for the Discovery and Developmental Therap
 eutics (DDT) and Cancer Immunology (CI) Joint Retreat\, “Breaking Immune
  Barriers: Translating Discovery into Tomorrow’s Therapies.” We invite
  you to take part in a day of collaboration\, insight and forward‑thinki
 ng discussion as we explore innovative research and chart the path from im
 mune‑focused discovery to transformative therapies of the future. Progra
 m Highlights Keynote Presentation: "Second Wave Modern Immunotherapy Drug 
 Development in Solid Tumors" Ryan Sullivan\, MD Director\, Cutaneous Medic
 al Oncology Program\; Associate Professor Mass General Brigham Cancer Inst
 itute\, Harvard Medical School The event will also feature faculty present
 ations\, cell therapy updates and flash talks from graduate student resear
 chers. Breakfast and lunch will be provided. Schedule Date: Tuesday\, Augu
 st 25\, 2026 8:00 a.m. Breakfast & Networking 8:30 a.m. Welcome and Progra
 m Updates 9:00 a.m. – 10:00 a.m. | Keynote Presentation 10:00 a.m. – 4
 :00 p.m. | Scientific Talks and Working Lunch with Graduate Student Flash 
 Talk Presentations\n\nSource: https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/E
 vent/6698/in-person---discovery-and-developmental-therapeutics-ddt-and-can
 cer-immunology-ci-joint-program-retreat---breaking-immune-barriers-transla
 ting-discovery-into-tomorrows-therapies/
LOCATION:Margret H. Rollins Room (R-P01) Rollins School of Public Health 1
 518 Clifton Road NE Atlanta \, Georgia 30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6698/in-person---disc
 overy-and-developmental-therapeutics-ddt-and-cancer-immunology-ci-joint-pr
 ogram-retreat---breaking-immune-barriers-translating-discovery-into-tomorr
 ows-therapies/
