SUMMARY:[Retreat] 2026 Cancer Biology T32 Training Program
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260827T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260827T140000
DTSTAMP:20260817T105227Z
UID:winship-2a0e433b04ca433eb77ff735@emory-seminars
DESCRIPTION:Program: Retreat\n\nSpeaker: 2026 Cancer Biology T32 Training 
 Program\n\nEvent type: Retreat\n\nPlease join us for the 3rd annual Cancer
  Biology T32 Training Program Retreat! The NIH T32 training grant supports
  both pre-doctoral and post-doctoral trainees within Winship\, promoting i
 nnovative and exciting research within multiple laboratories. This event w
 ill feature keynote speaker Melinda Bachini\, chief patient officer of the
  Cholangiocarcinoma Foundation\, in addition to talks from trainees suppor
 ted by this grant. We are excited to showcase all our trainees' exciting w
 ork and hope to see you there! RSVP HERE by August 24 Schedule 9:15 a.m. C
 heck-in\, coffee and refreshments 9:30 a.m. Welcome Message and Introducti
 on of Keynote Speaker David Yu\, MD\, PhD\, director\, Post-doctoral Train
 ing Program Sumin Kang\, PhD\, and Gregory Lesinski\, PhD\, MPH\, director
 s\, Pre-doctoral Training Program 9:45 a.m. Keynote Address – "Outlier: 
 The Patient Behind the Data" Melinda Bachini\, chief patient officer\, Cho
 langiocarcinoma Foundation 10:45 a.m. Break 11:00 a.m. Post-doctoral Train
 ee Talks Adedeji Adebayo\, DVM\, PhD\, MS\, Lisa Nieland\, PhD\, MS\, Chri
 stina Ramelow\, PhD\, MS\, and Nolan Tucker\, PhD 12:00 p.m. Lunch (provid
 ed) 1:00 p.m. Pre-doctoral Trainee Talks Anna Baj\, Alexis Dixon\, Ruby Fr
 eeman and Chloe Hope 2:00 p.m. Closing Remarks Alexis Dixon\n\nSource: htt
 ps://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6752/2026-cancer-biology-t32
 -training-program-retreat/
LOCATION:John H. Kauffman Auditorium (C5012\, 5th Floor Winship) Winship C
 ancer Institute 1365 Clifton Road NE\, Building C Atlanta \, Georgia 30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6752/2026-cancer-biol
 ogy-t32-training-program-retreat/
END:VEVENT
