BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Lectures and Training] Cure to Cancer Survivorship: A New Era of 
 Biomarkers\, Interventions\, and Care Models
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270206T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270206T130000
DTSTAMP:20260817T105227Z
UID:winship-e1b7a0bd26d889e8a34c0713@emory-seminars
DESCRIPTION:Program: Lectures and Training\n\nSpeaker: Cure to Cancer Surv
 ivorship: A New Era of Biomarkers\, Interventions\, and Care Models\n\nEve
 nt type: Lectures and Training\n\nOverview Cure to Cancer Survivorship: A 
 New Era of Biomarkers\, Interventions\, and Care Models is a one-day educa
 tional conference jointly sponsored by Winship Cancer Institute of Emory U
 niversity and Physicians’ Education Resource (PER®). Cancer survivorshi
 p is one of the most rapidly evolving areas in oncology. As treatment effi
 cacy improves across many tumor types\, the long-term physical\, psycholog
 ical\, and social impact of cancer management has emerged as an important 
 topic as part of overall cancer care. This inaugural program for oncologis
 ts and other health care professionals managing cancer features expert spe
 akers addressing cancer survivorship topics from screening through diagnos
 is\, treatment\, and long-term follow-up. Key program features will includ
 e expert presentations and holistic discussions on how to integrate surviv
 orship into clinical decision-making from the time of diagnosis\, dose del
 ivery\, and adherence optimization through lifestyle and supportive interv
 entions. Management of chronic debilitating toxicities\, such as fatigue a
 nd nausea\, and discussion of long-term efficacy and safety data for key t
 herapies and extended treatment regimens will also be reviewed. Specific t
 opics will include: Treatment selection\, balancing long-term efficacy wit
 h long-term safety and patient-reported outcomes Supportive physical care 
 during and after treatment Long-term adherence in the setting of extended 
 medical therapies: behavioral strategies\, lifestyle advice\, technology-e
 nabled tools\, and shared decision-making frameworks Target Audience This 
 educational activity is directed toward academic and community-based oncol
 ogists\, hematologists\, transplant physicians\, nurse practitioners (NPs)
 \, physician assistants (PAs)\, nurses\, and other health care professiona
 ls involved in the management of patients with cancer. Program Chair Neil 
 M. Iyengar\, MD Register Today\n\nSource: https://apps.winshipcancer.emory
 .edu/admin/Event/6760/cure-to-cancer-survivorship-a-new-era-of-biomarkers-
 interventions-and-care-models/
LOCATION:Loews Atlanta Hotel 1065 Peachtree Street NE Atlanta \, Georgia 3
 0309
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6760/cure-to-cancer-s
 urvivorship-a-new-era-of-biomarkers-interventions-and-care-models/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Lectures and Training] 2027 Georgia Cancer Summit
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270209T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270209T150000
DTSTAMP:20260817T105227Z
UID:winship-4cfd6233b5e42a086407388c@emory-seminars
DESCRIPTION:Program: Lectures and Training\n\nSpeaker: 2027 Georgia Cancer
  Summit\n\nEvent type: Lectures and Training\n\n2027 Georgia Cancer Summit
  Transforming Cancer Control: Rural Support in Action The Georgia Cancer S
 ummit is co-hosted by Winship Cancer Institute of Emory University\, Georg
 ia CORE\, the Georgia Department of Public Health\, the American Cancer So
 ciety\, and the Georgia Cancer Control Consortium. Purpose The goal of the
  2027 Georgia Cancer Summit is to catalyze efforts to reduce barriers to a
 ccess to prevention\, screening and quality cancer care for all Georgians.
  Summit participants will: Learn best practices to advance cancer preventi
 on\, control\, and research throughout Georgia Enhance understanding of sp
 ecial challenges for cancer prevention & control among rural populations H
 ear about challenges in the current government funding environment and lea
 rn best practices to establish partnerships and take action at the local a
 nd state levels Be able to network with other organizations that may lead 
 to new partnerships Identify ways your organization can get more involved 
 in advancing Georgia’s comprehensive cancer control objectives Audience 
 The Georgia Cancer Summit is for public health professionals\, health care
  providers\, health advocates\, researchers\, community-based organization
 s\, and others committed to improving cancer health equity in Georgia thro
 ugh cancer prevention and control and community-engaged research.\n\nSourc
 e: https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6758/2027-georgia-canc
 er-summit/
LOCATION:University of Georgia Tifton Campus Conference Center 15 R D C Rd
  Tifton \, Georgia 31794
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6758/2027-georgia-can
 cer-summit/
END:VEVENT
